---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JournalList from '../../components/JournalList.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const entries = (await getCollection('journal')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research journal"
  description="Long-form findings from the Restless coordination research programme."
  active="journal"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>What changed<br /><em>our operating theory.</em></h1>
    <p>These are research notes, not product mythology. Each one has one thesis, exact source locators and a boundary on what it can support.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="journal-preview journal-index">
    <JournalList entries={entries} />
  </section>

  <section class="journal-method">
    <h2>How to read the record.</h2>
    <p>Observed facts, product decisions and open questions remain distinct. Controlled test-world output is evidence about a mechanism, never market demand. A rejected or invalid result stays in the record when it changes the next decision.</p>
    <a class="underline-link" href="/research/corpus/">Inspect coverage and deferrals <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
